    "intro_html":  "Tsukune are the Japanese meatballs you find on skewers at a yakitori counter, glazed in a sweet soy tare until they shine. Ours bake on sheet pans and then get tossed in the same glaze, which is faster and does not require a charcoal grill in your kitchen. Over rice with sesame and green onion, each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e720 calories and 43 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$2.50\u003c/strong\u003e.",
